out being  in a boat and being in the dark that  didn't sit well with him but with a  little arm-twisting and the added  element of him not wanting to look like  a [ __ ] in front of his friend I was  able to get pirates on our agenda that  evening as we queued I could see my  brother starting to get nervous he does  this thing where he runs his hands  through his hair when he's nervous and  right now his hair was a mess  there was something different about this  time though sure he did this during all  the lines for rides he was nervous to go  on but he just had this look in his eye  that was somehow different when we were  standing in line for pirates I told  myself that he'd get over it once he'd  experienced the ride once and tried not  to make a big deal out of it he kept on  asking me questions how many drops are  there do you get wet does it go  pitch-black  will the pirates touch you I just about  couldn't take any more incessant  pestering by the time we'd reached the  front of the line  our boat pulled into the station and we  filled in sticking with the usual  seating arrangement of Nick Shawn than  me but then Shawn jumps out of his seat  and crossed over to the right side of  the station come on I told him this  rides nothing then his friend Nick  jumped out and offered to skip the ride  with him great my 1 bargaining tool was  gone  you can go we'll meet you by that I  considered this for a moment mom would  probably kill me if she knew I'd let  them go by themselves still we'd waited  for so long and this was one of my  favorite rides he was 11 years old now  and they were together what's the worst  that could happen  fine but you stay together and meet me  right by the exit and with that Nick and  Sean disappeared into the dark of the  synthetic bayou  my boat took off I was in the third row  in front of me there were two parents  and their young son in the front row was  occupied by two kids about Shawn's age  and their mom seeing them momentarily  