s broken or if the  entire ride system was done my biggest  fear was getting stuck on the ride and  Shawn and Nick not knowing what to do  wandering off there was some chatter  from the other guests the kids asking  what would happen the parents and myself  trying to figure out what to do there  was no cell reception at one point we  decided to call out no response though I  knew it was a long shot we discussed the  possibility of a power outage and what  would happen if that were the case how  long would we be trapped down here was  it a good idea to go out on foot before  we could come to a decision suddenly the  power seemed to kick back on all at once  and that was when probably the most  terrifying thing happened the voice  chanting dead men tell no tales boomed  over us as a strobe light viciously  overloaded my retinas the shock of these  two events would have been enough to  give someone a heart attack but what I  saw in the light is something that still  chills me to this day we were at the  shipwreck scene if you're not familiar  with the ride there's a portion where a  strobe light occasionally illuminates  the image  Elton gripping the steering wheel of a  destroyed vessel during a heavy  rainstorm the scene is mostly a dark  silhouette in front of the stormy night  sky but when the lightning struck there  was someone standing there staring at us  and I can tell you right now this was no  animatronic I obviously didn't get a  great look at him in that short split  second but he had a big bushy beard it  was hard to tell if he was even dressed  to fit the ride or if he was just some  guy in the dark jacket despite having  only seen him for a fraction of a second  I couldn't get his fiery stare out of my  head almost immediately after this the  lights shut back off in the audio slowed  to his stop it was pretty clear at this  point that they were having power issues  again if you're not familiar with the  rides layout the shipwreck scene is  normally only 